WEBVTT

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.040
<b>Job Fair

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.040
<b>Your choices are unlimited

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Your choices are unlimited

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.970
<b><i>Run With The Wind</i></b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.940
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.190
What a carefree bunch.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.830
<b>Inbox</b>

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.830
<b>AKECHI Co. new graduate hires
Initial screening results</b>

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.470
What you said was truly remarkable.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:38.220
I understand the fondness you have for Aotake.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.480
How many times have you said that?

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.580
I was moved, too.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:46.930
I usually ignore what you say 
since you use such difficult Japanese,

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.520
but I understood exactly
what you said this morning.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.210
You've been ignoring me?

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:57.050
He said he wasn't sure
if we were friends, though.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.060
Neither are we.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.100
Oh, right.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.530
That guy was a jerk, though.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.540
Aren't you embarrassed to run at their level?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.660
We have to, at least, beat him.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.630
Um...

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.760
Huh?

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.750
I'm sorry.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:19.660
Why?

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.170
Because he...

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.130
It's not your fault.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.930
He's just a jerk.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.560
Well, some way or another, they're acquaintances.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.520
Don't be too hard on him.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.170
That doesn't matter.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.230
Kakeru's our friend now. Right?

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.690
You're supposed to agree!

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.850
Yes!

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.100
Yes, Shindo?

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.370
I'm gonna try to run in the Hakone Ekiden!

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.700
At first, I just thought
my parents would be happy

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.960
if they saw me runnin' in the Hakone Ekiden,

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.210
but with fast guys like
Haiji and Kakeru around,

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.830
I feel like we could actually do it.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:08.850
But like that guy from the Sport
University said, we're extras.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.150
No, we're a burden to—

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.600
Enough already!

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.350
I don't wanna be like that!

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:19.900
We've chosen to stay here, so let's run!

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.780
I'll make my own choices of my own free will!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.370
In other words?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.450
I'll make it into the Hakone
Ekiden on my own strength!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.140
Well said!

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.580
Thank you!

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.660
Yeah!

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.040
Let's get lots of girls, Shindo!

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.210
Huh? But I have a girlfriend.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.840
What?! You do?

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.650
Don't get so excited.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:49.300
Just so you know, I'm still
opposed to running in the Ekiden!

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.730
Quit acting like we'll all be running!

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:53.950
Right, Musa?

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.150
Musa!

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.370
I'll run, too.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:04.630
Shindo's words touched my heart.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:08.010
You're so moved, you've lost your mind.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:11.480
Another toast!

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.630
Yeah!

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.290
<b>With all your might</b>

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.290
<b>You can do it</b>

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.380
We won't let anyone beat us!

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.640
We'll get tons of girls!

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.800
I'm goin' to Hakone!

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.130
I'll start by buying shoes!

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.370
For my health!

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.030
You can't peer pressure me!

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:26.390
Um, I never said I'd run...

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.070
How about you, Kakeru?

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.480
I...

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.940
I never said I'd run.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.960
I'd like to become a better speaker.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.030
What kind of reason is that?

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.870
Are you a comedian?

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:50.740
Then I'll toast to the resolve of my friends!

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.950
I never said...

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.410
The mountains of Hakone...

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.620
...that I would run.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.740
The steepest in the world!

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.630
<b><i>The Ones Not Chosen</i></b>

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:03.380
Haiji.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.050
<b>4/29 
Tokyo Sports Uni track meet!!</b>

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.050
What is this track meet?

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.460
Competitions take place
in the spring and summer.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:14.720
University- or corporate-sponsored
races are held practically every week.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.880
Track meets are one of them.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.830
Why do we have to run in that?

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.770
I explained that the other day.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.530
Not everyone gets to run.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.130
You have to qualify for the qualifier.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.650
You need an official record
of 5,000 m in less than 16:30

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:36.270
or 10,000 m in less than 30:00.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.460
Oh.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.420
I only got that you were kinda mad.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.500
You'd better learn to be a better speaker.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:50.380
I see. In order to do that,
we'll have to run in track meets.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.720
That's right.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:07:02.770
<b>Kakeru 14:53:54 

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.570
So that's why our goal is around 16 minutes.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.890
Looks like you're down to half your numbers.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.370
It seems like it'd be faster
to change the flow of time

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.770
than improve our running ability.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:06.020
Could you extend my deadline, then?

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.350
You're doing software development work again?

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:16.370
Naturally, there will be more
than just the one meet in April.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.980
We'll try multiple times in May and June.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:21.220
We just need to achieve
our target time eventually.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:50.950
Not going to sleep?

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.860
Are we really running
the Tokyo Sports Uni meet?

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:00.200
They're no match for them.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.330
At least wait until May.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.290
What point is there in putting it off?

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.410
They'll just get hurt.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.020
Why force them to face reality?

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:12.720
They're amateurs.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.610
Are you sure?

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:16.410
Huh?

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.600
Are only the chosen allowed to participate?

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:23.670
Is that what running is about?

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.490
We're talking about a competitive sport.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:34.790
You're right.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:39.480
But that's why we need to face reality.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.790
Otherwise, we can't even try.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:43.540
Hakone isn't a dream.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.620
It's reality.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.660
What?!

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:03.710
I said we're meeting
outside this evening at five.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:06.260
But we just got back from running!

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.920
The morning jog is a warm-up.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.730
Starting today, we'll start holding
proper practices in the evening.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.500
We're officially starting.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.910
Are we done with class by then?

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.750
It's probably fine for us to ditch.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:21.790
Shindo.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.870
Could you teach me about shoes later?

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.620
Of course.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.870
This is crazy. You're crazy.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:33.130
You're acting like a track and field team!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.840
But we are.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.300
Say something!

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.160
Huh? Oh...

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.560
I'll pass. I've got a seminar today.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:46.660
You can't reschedule?

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:48.600
Reschedule?

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:54.270
I'll have to reschedule my entire life, too.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.570
Will you take responsibility for that?

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.090
I've rescheduled my life like crazy.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:09.240
What are these? Voodoo dolls?

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:12.570
My hands keep looking for cigarettes.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.090
I made those while trying to distract myself.

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:18.110
When did you stop smoking?

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.820
Don't tell me it was the day 
Haiji brought up Hakone.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:24.260
Of course not.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:27.170
It's not easy to quit.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.980
It hasn't been a week yet.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.560
That means you've quit for now!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.730
Shut up.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.390
You should be glad.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:36.730
You used to complain every day.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.660
In other words...

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.040
this means you're running, right?

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.870
Despite staying up all night
to work all the time,

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.320
you're participating in our morning jogs

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:53.130
because you want to run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.300
I don't dislike running.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:58.540
Give me a break!

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.480
If you join them...

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.130
But ability's a different story.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:04.930
Huh?

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:10.780
Don't worry. I'm not taking Haiji seriously.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.710
I'm seriously doing it for my health.

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:15.020
It's a good opportunity.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.330
What? Lucky!

00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:36.420
Aren't they nice?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.220
Will new shoes make us faster?

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.160
I'm sure they will.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:44.770
If we want to buy shoes,
we'll have to go drinking less.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.610
Maybe we can do something short term.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:48.930
A job, huh?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.890
I don't wanna work...

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:51.890
I'm back.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.070
Hey.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:53.930
Welcome home.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:55.310
Sorry. I'll get changed.

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:58.390
Third-years have seminars.

00:11:58.390 --> 00:11:59.740
Must be hard.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:05.190
Haiji is with Yuki and Nico-chan Senpai.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:08.240
King's not showing up, after all.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:12.760
He's been freaking out lately.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:16.250
<b>202</b>

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.870
Maybe he's setting his sights too high.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:17.750
Who wouldn't?

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.210
Prince is over there.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:26.370
Between you and me, which
of us do you think is truly free?

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.890
We'll leave once Shindo gets here.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:34.900
Nira, you wanna come?

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.390
And Prince.

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:41.570
<b>Feeble</b>

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:41.150
Could you please not treat us
like we're on the same level?

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.670
This place is kinda dismal.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:13:01.120
Even though we're the track team,
we can't use the university's track.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:05.120
The university's track is used
by all kinds of teams and clubs.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.160
It's all about the pecking order.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.470
Haiji.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:09.550
Yes, Musa?

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.970
You said we'd be easing into practice.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:15.420
Does that mean we'll be running slowly?

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.440
That's right.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.710
If you suddenly start running,
you'll hurt yourself.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.900
Before practice, we'll start
with a one-hour run.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.360
One hour?!

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.840
Haiji.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.820
Yes, Prince?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.810
Isn't that just practice?

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:29.990
Let's go.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.960
That's what you call ignoring someone.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:39.290
You're the only one who understands me.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:42.700
Are you <i>trying</i> to descend to his level?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.890
We'll do a fixed-pace run.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.300
What's a fixed-pace run?

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:53.930
It means running at a constant pace.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.020
It's good for endurance training.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.840
Don't push yourselves too hard at first.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.650
Focus on completing the run.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.360
Yeah!

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.170
There's no need to strain
yourselves by running too fast.

00:14:07.170 --> 00:14:11.660
Focus on maintaining a pace
you can run at for a long time.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.550
All right, first group.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:14.850
Yeah!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:20.780
We're like a real team.

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.550
You can't be serious.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.380
Right, Nira?

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:36.880
You're one of them, too?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:40.060
What's so great about it?

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.120
Huh?

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.150
About running.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:46.860
I don't get it. I'm an amateur.

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:56.540
As long as I don't,
there's nothing I can do about it.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.990
Don't tell me I'll understand
once I start running.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.270
Second group.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:13.010
Everyone's different.

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:15.810
<i>But in my case...</i>

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:17.110
Go!

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.190
No fair!

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:32.660
<i>Are only the chosen allowed to participate?</i>

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:42.010
<i>Is that what running is about?</i>

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.470
That's all for today.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:56.320
Tomorrow, we'll incorporate
build-up runs. Keep that in mind.

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.680
You're adding more?!

00:15:57.980 --> 00:15:59.770
Build-up runs?

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:03.440
It means gradually increasing
your pace to a sprint.

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.240
What's the objective of that practice?

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.780
Working your heart and lungs.

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.810
There's no point unless 
you're having trouble breathing.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:13.690
I see.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.700
Was Haiji smiling at the end?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.140
Looked that way to me.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:21.160
He's an ogre.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:21.990
Huh?

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:28.040
An ogre doesn't understand how people feel.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:32.440
Prince, have you lost even more weight?

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:36.800
Maybe it's my imagination,
but he looks semi-transparent to me.

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:39.840
I'm trying to become incorporeal.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:42.970
It's the only way I can exist in this world.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.830
Stand up, Prince.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:48.690
We're jogging back to Aotake.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:52.510
I'll explain the rest to you tonight.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:53.670
No, thanks.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:57.820
Despite everything, even
Prince is going along with it.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.340
So are you.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.740
You never told me your answer.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.080
You're persistent.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.750
Yeah, but...

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.340
Well, when I'm running...

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:16.460
Only when I'm running, I feel clean.

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.800
Pure white.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.400
I can leave all the stuff I'm carrying behind.

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:28.310
For just a moment, I feel perfectly clean.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:33.280
But I'm already clean.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.360
You piss me off.

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.710
What? That's the reason?

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:40.910
<i>That's</i> the reason? Huh?

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.120
<b>202</b>

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.970
<b>Inbox</b>

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:04.520
<b>From: Dream Top Co. recruiter/NTo: Sakaguchi Yohei
Subject: Regarding initial screening results
Dear Mr. Sakaguchi Yohei,
Thank you for applying for a position
with our business department.
Unfortunately, your school records
did not pass our screening this time.
Good luck with your future endeavors.
Please understand that we cannot answer
any questions regarding the screening results.
Dream Top Co. Recruiter</b>

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.780
What?

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.760
How about after this?

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.590
You're going to keep running?

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:27.540
Yeah. There's not much time before the meet.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.040
Besides, there's something I want to try.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.220
Is it okay if I go jogging tonight?

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.880
Of course. Watch out for traffic.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:37.970
All right.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:39.580
Me, too.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:41.890
If Joji's going, so will I.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.130
I'll go, too.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:44.690
Let's get changed.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:45.550
Yeah!

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.620
I'll pass. I'm overworked.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:50.900
Sorry, but I'm going to relax, too.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.140
They're becoming independent. That's good.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:56.820
Where's Prince?

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.600
I forgot him in the yard.

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.360
He'll catch a cold!

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.850
How about you? You're not gonna run?

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:03.620
Huh?

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:06.630
It's written all over your face
that you haven't had your fill.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:10.140
Kakeru.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.210
Help me make dinner.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:15.620
Haiji—

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:17.670
King, you're home?

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.740
Just how much are you guys practicing?

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.880
You guys sure have
a weird way of having fun.

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:26.340
I'm hungry. Where's dinner?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.510
Soon. What's up?

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.980
It's nothing.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.520
Okay.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:36.730
You're lucky to have guys who want to run.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:37.660
What?

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.190
I'm sure you have plenty of time.

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:42.450
Run as much as you want.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:43.790
I'm taking a bath!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.830
What?!

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:55.540
What? All of us?

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.150
Of course.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:59.800
From now on, you're all forbidden from working.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.300
And get some running clothes.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:07.320
Prince's denim is out of the question.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:12.370
I've never needed a track
suit before in my life.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.480
You can't wear track suits, either.

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:18.320
Make sure have towels
and bring a change of clothes, too.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:20.680
Changing your clothes
regularly is an important part

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:22.280
of maintaining your physical condition.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:26.370
When you're practicing every day,
you won't have time for anything else.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:29.190
You'll be able to save up more
than enough off your allowances.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.610
And...

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.620
Hey!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.170
I'm not doing nothing but practice every day.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:41.800
Sorry, but I've got my own life to live.

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.380
King...

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:42.670
Next time: "The Emperor's New Clothes."
